 ```
 
+##### limit
+
+Specifies the maximum number of ranges to return, defaults to no limit. When
+the header contains more ranges than `limit` (after `combine`, if enabled), a
+single range from the lowest start to the highest end is returned instead.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(100, 'bytes=0-1,10-11,50-55', { limit: 2 })
+// => [
+//      { start: 0, end: 55 }
+//    ]
+```
+
